The value became reachable in the previous PR; nothing reached it. This gives
it producers.

`no_candidate_construct_if_empty(candidates)` is the producer helper. Its
argument MUST be what the pass's own scan FOUND -- the patterns, the call
sites, the bindings -- and never what the pass finally EMITTED. The two differ
exactly where it matters: a linker emitting one symbol per candidate is silent
precisely when it found none, but a linker emitting only PAIRING edges is also
silent when it found candidates on one side and none on the other, and there
the construct IS present.

MEASURED on a self-survey, not reasoned: no_candidate_construct 0 -> 6,
unreported 11 -> 5.

Drained (scanned, genuinely found nothing): crypto-flow, graphql-resolver,
grpc, message-queue, pyffi, solidity-abi.

NOT drained, and this is the finding: annotation-convention, di-resolution,
ipc, wasm-bindgen, message-dispatch found candidates and emitted nothing
anyway. They stay `unreported` = CANNOT DETERMINE, because THE AXIS HAS NO
VALUE FOR "candidates found, relation not established". That population was
invisible before -- undifferentiated inside unreported -- and is now countable
at five. Declaring a value for it needs a producer, or it becomes the trap
prerequisite_absent is already in.

wasm-bindgen and pyffi could not be ASKED the question until a candidate
accumulator was added: both scanned per file and discarded what they found.
Anchoring on emitted edges would have had them declare the construct absent
while it sat there unpaired -- the WI-finij defect committed a second time by
the people fixing it.

Anchoring on the candidate set is also robust to misreading a linker: ipc and
annotation-convention were classified as symbol-per-candidate and actually
gate emission behind a match (ipc has a `continue` before its symbol append).
The rule gave the right answer regardless, because it never asks what the pass
emitted.

crypto-flow and message-dispatch take the claim on their early bail, whose
`if not all_writes or not all_reads` conflates "found nothing" with "found one
side"; it fires only when both are empty.

mypy: a bare `list` annotation breached the ratchet 667 -> 668 and is now
list[tuple[str, str, int]], which then exposed that the concatenation beside it
mixed element types and had only passed because the bare annotation made it
Any. Back to 667.

